{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793179457,"nonce":"BCipj+mUtsj7Vx9mTJ+NwrJBQrM=","title":"Provide browser Jam rooms without desktop-native FFI or competing document ownership","message":"The landing-page extension audit found Jam is a built-in feature, not a RayScript extension. Its document and room operations call rayscript HDLL primitives directly through NativeJam, which are not staged in the browser bundle. In a connected workspace EditorDocuments already owns CodeEditorState.onTransaction/onUndo, and JamFeature.begin deliberately refuses another owner. Calling native Jam from a browser cannot supply a working room and must not trap the page.\n\nBuild an explicit browser/session Jam transport and reconcile it with the existing workspace CRDT projection/undo ownership. Preserve per-author undo, names/cursors, follow, history-diff attribution, document/tab selection semantics, recovery identities and private invite credentials. Use the shared native/jam protocol where appropriate and keep network work outside UI threads. Test browser/native peers, multiple browser peers, reconnect, room lifecycle, explicit leave and cleanup. Do not represent ordinary workspace text sync as complete Jam presence/follow support.\n\nThe landing pass keeps a clear desktop-availability message and prevents unsupported browser starts while the three script extensions (Git, Markdown, Rayzor) use their supervised session processes. Related browser epic ae3a156433377383faa317d5da1f34e6eab10f9a6e0d0ab0456fc0e0277a8382 and landing issue 66e2d7d. This remains separate from media streaming and production Cloudflare deployment.","files":null}]}